Any block floats (plan P3-15): a figure whose body is a table floats right at 45% of the measure, its caption beneath it, the text beside it narrowed.

#!figure(label: "tbl-float", style: {place: {float: "right", width: "45%"}})
#!table(cols: 2)
Name | Qty
Alpha | 2
Beta | 3
#table!
A floated table.
#figure!

The paragraph beside the floated table wraps around it: its first lines break at the narrowed width, the ones below the float's bottom at the full measure again, as for an image float; the figure is laid out on its own, a flow root, at the width it asked for.

After the float, @tbl-float is referenced as usual.
